"""Colour by number on paintings, made for an older player.

A picture is a grid of cells, each with a number; the palette at the
bottom has one big button per number. Pick a colour, tap its cells.
- Cells of the chosen number are tinted and their numbers bold, so they
  are easy to find; a cell of another number cannot be painted.
- The buttons on the right carry drawn icons, no words: back, zoom in,
  zoom out (down to the whole picture on screen), in small steps, "whole picture" (one
  tap fits the picture to the screen, the next one goes back to the
  same zoom and place), "where?" (puts the
  nearest unpainted cell of the chosen colour in the middle), undo, and
  "look" (the finished picture while held). Drag to scroll.
- A tap paints the whole connected area of that number at once (a
  large sky is one tap).
- Every button and every painting tap gives a short buzz, a wrong cell
  does not (one
  emission hook on GtkButton "pressed" covers all buttons, dialogs
  included); there is no timer, no score, no ads.
- Progress is saved after every tap, so a picture can wait for tomorrow;
  the program starts on the last picture, unless it is finished, and the
  gallery opens at that picture's card.

The gallery runs from easier to harder as it scrolls down: paintings in
64, 96 and 128 cells along the long side with up to 16, 24 and 28
colours. 128 is about the limit for this tablet: a tap there takes some
200 ms. To stay quick, a tap redraws only the cells it changed, progress
is written a moment after the last tap, and gallery thumbnails are kept
as PNG files.

Pictures: the built-in ones in /usr/local/share/b8k/paint/, and any photo
put into ~/Раскраски (JPEG or PNG), which is turned into a picture of 64
cells along the long side and up to 16 colours the first time it is shown.

New pictures: "+ Найти" in the gallery header searches Wikidata for
paintings (items that are an instance of painting and have an image), by
artist, title or what is painted, in Russian as well; the pictures
themselves come from Wikimedia Commons, where every file is under a free
licence and most paintings are in the public domain. A tap on a result
shows it large with its artist and year, as it will look painted at the
chosen cell size (a tap on it shows the painting itself); the conversion
is the one of paint/make-paintings.py. "Загрузить" keeps it in
~/.local/share/b8k-paint/downloaded/, shown in its own gallery section, where "✕ Убрать" takes it out again. Only
https requests to wikidata.org, commons.wikimedia.org and the Wikimedia
image hosts are made.
